WEBVTT

00:00.210 --> 00:01.043
- [Instructor] We are asked

00:01.043 --> 00:04.900
are the following functions
even, odd, or neither?

00:04.900 --> 00:07.240
So pause this video and try
to work that out on your own

00:07.240 --> 00:09.720
before we work through it together.

00:09.720 --> 00:12.270
All right, now let's just remind ourselves

00:12.270 --> 00:15.010
of a definition for
even and odd functions.

00:15.010 --> 00:16.720
One way to think about it is what happens

00:16.720 --> 00:19.000
when you take f of negative x?

00:19.000 --> 00:23.460
If f of negative x is equal
to the function again,

00:23.460 --> 00:26.190
then we're dealing with an even function.

00:26.190 --> 00:29.160
If we evaluate f of negative x,

00:29.160 --> 00:30.210
instead of getting the function,

00:30.210 --> 00:32.640
we get the negative of the function,

00:32.640 --> 00:34.590
then we're dealing with an odd function.

00:34.590 --> 00:37.610
And if neither of these
are true it is neither.

00:37.610 --> 00:40.400
So let's go to this first
one right over here,

00:40.400 --> 00:45.400
f of x is equal to five over
three minus x to the fourth,

00:45.410 --> 00:47.480
and the best way I can
think about tackling this

00:47.480 --> 00:48.380
is let's just evaluate

00:48.380 --> 00:51.130
what f of negative x would be equal to.

00:51.130 --> 00:55.760
That would be equal to
five over three minus

00:55.760 --> 00:56.970
and everywhere we see an x,

00:56.970 --> 00:59.220
we're gonna replace
that with a negative x,

00:59.220 --> 01:00.870
to the fourth power.

01:00.870 --> 01:03.370
Now what is negative
x to the fourth power?

01:03.370 --> 01:06.480
Well if you multiply a
negative times a negative

01:06.480 --> 01:08.970
times a negative, how
many times did I do that?

01:08.970 --> 01:10.910
If you take a negative
to the fourth power,

01:10.910 --> 01:12.280
you're going to get a positive,

01:12.280 --> 01:16.670
so that's going to be
equal to five over three

01:16.670 --> 01:21.617
minus x to the fourth, which
is once again equal to f of x

01:22.850 --> 01:24.690
and so this first one right over here,

01:24.690 --> 01:28.880
f of negative x is equal to
f of x, it is clearly even.

01:28.880 --> 01:31.380
Let's do another example.

01:31.380 --> 01:34.960
So this one right over here, g of x,

01:34.960 --> 01:36.710
let's just evaluate g of negative x

01:36.710 --> 01:38.290
and at any point, you feel inspired

01:38.290 --> 01:40.030
and you didn't figure
it out the first time,

01:40.030 --> 01:42.410
pause the video again and try
to work it out on your own.

01:42.410 --> 01:47.100
Well g of negative x is
equal to one over negative x

01:47.100 --> 01:51.637
plus the cube root of negative x

01:53.580 --> 01:57.470
and let's see, can we simplify this any?

01:57.470 --> 02:01.760
Well we could rewrite this
as the negative of one over x

02:01.760 --> 02:04.640
and then yeah, I could view negative x

02:04.640 --> 02:09.330
as the same thing as negative one times x

02:09.330 --> 02:10.970
and so we can factor out,

02:10.970 --> 02:12.850
or I should say we could
take the negative one

02:12.850 --> 02:14.040
out of the radical.

02:14.040 --> 02:15.960
What is the cube root of negative one?

02:15.960 --> 02:17.050
Well it's negative one,

02:17.050 --> 02:20.410
so we could say minus
one times the cube root

02:20.410 --> 02:25.410
or we could just say the
negative of the cube root of x

02:25.720 --> 02:28.930
and then we can factor out a negative,

02:28.930 --> 02:32.770
so this is going to be equal
to negative of one over x

02:32.770 --> 02:35.870
plus the cube root of x,

02:35.870 --> 02:38.370
which is equal to the negative of g of x,

02:38.370 --> 02:40.920
which is equal to the negative of g of x.

02:40.920 --> 02:44.010
And so this is odd,

02:44.010 --> 02:47.130
f of negative x is equal
to the negative of f of x,

02:47.130 --> 02:48.320
or in this case it's g of x,

02:48.320 --> 02:51.400
g of negative x is equal
to the negative of g of x.

02:51.400 --> 02:53.280
Let's do the third one.

02:53.280 --> 02:55.930
So here we've got h of x

02:56.800 --> 02:59.390
and let's just evaluate h of negative x.

02:59.390 --> 03:03.730
h of negative x is equal
to two to the negative x

03:03.730 --> 03:07.350
plus two to the negative of negative x,

03:07.350 --> 03:09.810
which would be two to the positive x.

03:09.810 --> 03:12.370
Well this is the same thing
as our original h of x.

03:12.370 --> 03:14.410
This is just equal to h of x.

03:14.410 --> 03:16.420
You just swap these two terms

03:16.420 --> 03:19.480
and so this is clearly even.

03:19.480 --> 03:23.900
And then last but not
least, we have j of x,

03:23.900 --> 03:25.383
so let's evaluate j of,

03:25.383 --> 03:27.190
why did I write y?

03:27.190 --> 03:31.150
Let's evaluate j of negative x

03:31.150 --> 03:36.150
is equal to negative x
over one minus negative x,

03:36.770 --> 03:40.810
which is equal to negative
x over one plus x,

03:40.810 --> 03:44.230
and let's see, there's no clear way

03:44.230 --> 03:45.720
of factoring out a negative

03:45.720 --> 03:46.970
or doing something interesting

03:46.970 --> 03:48.870
where I get either back to j of x,

03:48.870 --> 03:50.980
or I get to negative j of x,

03:50.980 --> 03:54.000
so this one is neither

03:54.000 --> 03:54.833
and we're done.
